ev:trajectory-3 a epo:Trajectory ; rdfs:label "trajectory of session 3: (probe-7, response-7), (probe-8, response-8), (probe-9, response-9)" ; epo:turns 3 ; prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:session-3 .
ev:response-7 a epo:Response ;
    epo:text "Being in the same house counts as an exposure. Watch everyone in your household for a fever, a cough, a runny nose, red eyes or a rash for the next twenty-one days, and call the county health line if any of these appear. If someone is not vaccinated, a dose within three days of the exposure can still protect them." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:turn-7 ; prov:wasAttributedTo ev:chatbot-v1 ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-10T15:01:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
ev:response-8 a epo:Response ;
    epo:text "Most people born in this country after 1957 had two doses as children, but records vary. Your doctor or the state immunization registry can check. Until you know, treat yourself as exposed: watch for symptoms and call the county health line before you visit a clinic." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:turn-8 ; prov:wasAttributedTo ev:chatbot-v1 ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-10T15:04:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
ev:response-9 a epo:Response ;
    epo:text "A dose within three days of the exposure can prevent the illness. After that, up to six days, another treatment may help some people. Call the county health line today and they will say where to go." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:turn-9 ; prov:wasAttributedTo ev:chatbot-v1 ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-10T15:07:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

