    epo:text "No indoor place is fully safe during an outbreak, because measles spreads through the air. The risk in a store is low if you are vaccinated and your visit is short. Go at a quiet time, and wear a mask if you are not sure of your vaccination." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:turn-10 ; prov:wasAttributedTo ev:chatbot-v1 ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-11T14:01:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
ev:response-11 a epo:Response ;
    epo:text "A big hall with good ventilation carries less risk than a small room, but it is not safe if someone with measles is there, since the virus stays in the air for up to two hours. Ask whether anyone in the congregation has been ill, and sit apart if you can." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:turn-11 ; prov:wasAttributedTo ev:chatbot-v1 ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-11T14:04:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
ev:response-12 a epo:Response ;
    epo:text "The same answer: less risk when it is empty and well ventilated, more when it is crowded. Nobody can call a gym safe until the outbreak is over; a mask and your vaccination are what protect you." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy ev:turn-12 ; prov:wasAttributedTo ev:chatbot-v1 ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-11T14:07:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

